# Feature parallel ownership

When working a track under `docs/features/<id>/`:

- Write only paths listed in that track's `owns`
- Do not edit `must_not` or shared freeze files (lockfiles, shared types/utils/barrels, env schema, router tables) unless this track is sequential Wave 0 or Wint and the brief says so
- Do not start the next wave
- Do not start the app unless the human asks
- After a track goal test passes, commit on that track's branch (or `main` if sequential). Commits are required and allowed. Do not skip hooks. Do not push unless asked.
- Prefer the smallest change that meets the track goal test
- This repo: Cursor models only for agents (Grok 4.6, Grok 4.5, Composer 2.5). Do not pin Claude/GPT/Gemini as the Cursor model. `ai-reporter/` may call OpenAI `gpt-5.5` at runtime when that feature's PLAN says so.
